3,Karata-Tukita language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/karata_tukita_language,"The Karata-Tukita language, commonly known as Karata (кӏкӏирлӏи), is an endangered Andic language belonging to the Avar-Andic subgroup of the Northeast Caucasian (Nakh-Daghestanian) language family. [1][2] It is spoken primarily in the villages of Karata and Tukita (also spelled Tokita) in the Akhvakhsky and Khazavyurt districts of southern Dagestan, Russia, within a rugged ...",Karata,Nakh-Daghestanian
